#1. Insertion sort 




Pick → Compare → Shift → Insert → Repeat

Pick: Select the next element.
Compare: Check the elements on its left.
Shift: Move bigger elements right.
Insert: Put the selected element in its correct position.
Repeat: Continue until the array is sorted.



arr=[10,30,40,20]
for i in range(1,len(arr)):
  key=arr[i]
  j=i-1
  while j>=0 and arr[j]>key:
    arr[j+1]=arr[j]
    j-=1
  arr[j+1]=key
print(arr)

Algorithm:

1. Pick a number (key).
2. Compare it with the numbers on its left.
3. Move bigger numbers one position to the right.
4. Insert key into the empty position.
5. Repeat until the array is sorted.
